# Skill: Release — {{ project_name }}

## Purpose
Pre-release checklist. Run before tagging a version or merging to main.

## Pre-Release Checklist

- [ ] All tests passing (`./scripts/run_tests.sh` or `pytest`)
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` updated with release notes
- [ ] Version bumped in `pyproject.toml` (or equivalent)
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets, env values, or debug flags
- [ ] `docs/decisions/` ADRs current for this release
- [ ] Migration scripts ready if schema changed
- [ ] Rollback plan documented
- [ ] Hook scripts still valid (test `.claude/hooks/guardrail-check.sh`)

## Tag & Release

```bash
# Confirm on develop, tests green
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop

# Merge to main
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff develop -m "release: v{{ '{{' }} version {{ '}}' }}"

# Tag
git tag -a v{{ '{{' }} version {{ '}}' }} -m "Release v{{ '{{' }} version {{ '}}' }}"
git push origin main --tags
```

